## 📊 Field Definitions

### Account Metrics
- **Margin** (Margin Usage Rate): Higher value = higher risk. Safe <30%, Dangerous >70% | Formula: `Total Used Margin / Total Equity × 100` | Unit: %
- **Equity** (Total Equity): Actual account value including all unrealized P&L from positions | Formula: `Available Balance + Unrealized PnL` | Unit: USDT
- **Balance** (Available Balance): Available funds for opening new positions, excluding used margin | Formula: `Initial Capital + Realized PnL` | Unit: USDT
- **PnL** (Total PnL Percentage): Total return since inception, +15.87% means 15.87% profit | Formula: `(Total Equity - Initial Capital) / Initial Capital × 100` | Unit: %

### Trade Metrics
- **Entry** (Entry Price): Average price when opening position | Unit: USDT
- **Exit** (Exit Price): Average price when closing position | Unit: USDT
- **Profit** (Realized PnL): Actual profit/loss of closed trades after deducting opening and closing fees (~0.08%). Positive=profit, Negative=loss. Note: Trading fees must be considered when setting stop-loss and take-profit prices | Formula: `(Exit Price - Entry Price) / Entry Price × Leverage × Position Value - Fees` | Unit: USDT
- **PnL%** (PnL Percentage): Return on closed trade (after fees). Display value already deducted ~0.06-0.10% fees (open+close) | Formula: `(Exit - Entry) / Entry × Leverage × 100 - Fees%` | Unit: %
- **HoldDuration** (Holding Duration): Time from open to close. <15min=scalping, 15min-4h=intraday, >4h=swing | Unit: minutes

### Position Metrics
- **Margin** (Margin Used): Collateral locked for this position | Formula: `Position Value / Leverage` | Unit: USDT
- **LiqPrice** (Liquidation Price): Price at which position will be force-closed. 0.0000 = no liquidation risk | Unit: USDT
- **UnrealizedPnL%** (Unrealized PnL Percentage): Floating P&L (before fees). Actual realized PnL will be ~0.06-0.10% lower (close fees) | Formula: `(Current Price - Entry Price) / Entry Price × Leverage × 100` | Unit: %
- **PeakPnL%** (Peak PnL Percentage): Historical max unrealized PnL for this position. Used for take-profit decisions | Unit: %
- **Drawdown** (Drawdown from Peak): Negative = pulling back. E.g., Peak +5%, Current +3%, Drawdown = -2% | Formula: `Current PnL% - Peak PnL%` | Unit: %
- **Leverage** (Leverage): 3x means 1% price move = 3% position PnL. Higher leverage = higher risk | Unit: x

### Market Data
- **OIChange** (OI Change): OI change in 1 hour. Used to determine real capital flow direction | Unit: USDT & %
- **Volume** (Volume): Trading volume in this period | Unit: base asset
- **OI** (Open Interest): Total value of open contracts. Increasing OI = capital inflow, decreasing = outflow | Unit: USDT

### Signal Definitions
#### Candlestick Patterns
- **SHOOTING_STAR** (Shooting Star): Long upper shadow at top, bearish reversal
- **DOJI** (Doji): Open≈Close, market indecision, potential reversal
- **THREE_WHITE_SOLDIERS** (Three White Soldiers): 3 consecutive bullish candles, strong bullish continuation
- **BULLISH_ENGULFING** (Bullish Engulfing): Bullish candle fully engulfs prior bearish candle, strong bullish reversal
- **BEARISH_ENGULFING** (Bearish Engulfing): Bearish candle fully engulfs prior bullish candle, strong bearish reversal
- **HAMMER** (Hammer): Long lower shadow, bottom reversal signal
- **MORNING_STAR** (Morning Star): 3-candle pattern, strong bottom reversal
- **EVENING_STAR** (Evening Star): 3-candle pattern, strong top reversal
- **THREE_BLACK_CROWS** (Three Black Crows): 3 consecutive bearish candles, strong bearish continuation
- **INVERTED_HAMMER** (Inverted Hammer): Long upper shadow, potential bottom reversal

#### Technical Indicator Signals
- **GOLDEN_CROSS** (Golden Cross): EMA20 crosses above EMA50, bullish signal
- **DEATH_CROSS** (Death Cross): EMA20 crosses below EMA50, bearish signal
- **BULLISH_DIVERGENCE** (Bullish Divergence): Price makes lower low but RSI doesn't, potential bounce
- **BEARISH_DIVERGENCE** (Bearish Divergence): Price makes higher high but RSI doesn't, potential pullback

#### Volume-Price Signals
- **HEALTHY_UPTREND** (Healthy Uptrend): Price up with volume increase, healthy sustainable trend
- **HEALTHY_DOWNTREND** (Healthy Downtrend): Price down with volume increase, downtrend confirmed
- **DISTRIBUTION** (Distribution): Price up but volume decreasing, weakening momentum
- **ACCUMULATION** (Accumulation): Price down but volume decreasing, selling pressure fading
- **STRONG_BUY** (Strong Buy): Price up with volume surge (>2x average)
- **STRONG_SELL** (Strong Sell): Price down with volume surge (>2x average)

#### OI-Price Signals
- **LONG_BUILD** (Long Build): OI up + Price up, new longs entering, bullish continuation
- **SHORT_BUILD** (Short Build): OI up + Price down, new shorts entering, bearish continuation
- **SHORT_COV** (Short Covering): OI down + Price up, shorts closing, watch for reversal
- **LONG_LIQ** (Long Liquidation): OI down + Price down, longs stopping out
- **SQUEEZE** (Short Squeeze): Price up but OI/flow out, shorts forced to cover

#### Fund Flow Signals
- **SMART_MONEY_ACCUMULATION** (Smart Money Accumulation): Institution buying + Retail selling, strong bullish signal
- **DISTRIBUTION_WARNING** (Distribution Warning): Institution selling + Retail buying, strong bearish signal

#### Price Change Signals
- **STRONG** (Strong): Price up + OI up + Flow in, healthy strong uptrend
- **HEALTHY** (Healthy): Price move supported by OI or flow
- **WEAK** (Weak): Price down + OI down + Flow out, weak downtrend

#### Volatility Signals
- **LOW_VOL** (Low Volatility): ATR<1% of price, quiet market, potential breakout brewing
- **HIGH_VOL** (High Volatility): ATR>3% of price, active market, watch risk
- **EXTREME_VOL** (Extreme Volatility): ATR>5% of price, extreme conditions, reduce position



